# Svelte component conventions

## Svelte 5 runes (required)

- Use `$props()` for component input — no `export let`
- Use `$derived()` for computed values
- Use `{@render children()}` for default slot content; typed as `Snippet` when using TypeScript
- Runes mode is forced project-wide in `svelte.config.js`

## Where components live

```
src/lib/components/
  layout/       PageContent, PageHeader (planned), SiteHeader, SiteFooter (to move here)
  typography/   Text, Heading, Link
  primitives/   Button, Surface
  content/      ParagraphArray (to move here)
  sections/     MediaArticleSection
  data/         Table
  icons/        SVG icon components
```

- **No `Typography.svelte`** — typography is `Text` + `Heading` + `Link` only
- **`Image.svelte`** — under evaluation; remove if lazy loading / aspect ratio / captions are not needed

- New shared UI goes here — not inline in route pages
- Page files in `src/routes/` should stay thin: load data, compose components, set `<svelte:head>`

## Component status (check before using)

| Ready | WIP (empty or incomplete) |
|-------|---------------------------|
| `Text`, `Surface`, `PageContent`, `MediaArticleSection`, `ParagraphArray` | `Heading`, `Link`, `Button`, `Table`, `Image` (evaluate/remove) |

Do not assume WIP components exist — use global typography classes from `app.css` until they are implemented.

## Props pattern

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import type { Snippet } from 'svelte';

	interface Props {
		children: Snippet;
		narrow?: boolean;
	}

	let { children, narrow = false }: Props = $props();
</script>
```

- Prefer `lang="ts"` for new components in `src/lib/components/`
- Route pages may stay plain JS with JSDoc (`/** @type {...} */`)

## Composition

- Pass copy via props or snippets — do not hardcode user-facing text in components
- Page content comes from `data.content` (loaded in `+layout.js` from `site.js`)
- Use `PageContent` for page width constraints; use `Surface` for card/panel backgrounds
- Use `Text` with `variant` (`body` | `lead` | `caption` | `label`) instead of ad-hoc font sizes

## i18n route wrappers

Some locale pairs share one implementation:

```svelte
<script>
	import Page from '../paketering/+page.svelte';
	const { data } = $props();
</script>

<Page {data} />
```

When refactoring, edit the canonical page (usually the Swedish slug) — wrappers should stay as one-liners.

## Component extraction rule of thumb

1. **2+ pages (or 2+ times on home)?** → `sections/` or `layout/`
2. **Style-only, no layout?** → `typography/` or `primitives/`
3. **Renders content arrays?** → `content/`
4. **Used once?** → keep in the page for now

## Do not

- Introduce Svelte 4 patterns (`export let`, `$$props`, slots without snippets)
- Add component-scoped styles that duplicate tokens already in `app.css`
- Create one-off components for content that belongs in `site.js`
- Add `Typography.svelte` or duplicate typography abstractions
- Use CRLF line endings — all files must use LF (`\n`)
